  "content": "\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-fill\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-dark-gray-background-color has-background wp-element-button\" href=\"/zh-tw/\">繁體中文</a></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-fill\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-bright-blue-background-color has-background wp-element-button\" href=\"/zh-cn/\">简体中文</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">HokkienLang is a space for exploring <strong>Hokkien</strong> through <strong>Tangliengim</strong> (<em>pronounced Tung-LEE-eng-im</em>) — a writing system designed to make Hokkien pronunciation, tones, and sound changes easier to visualise.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Tangliengim?</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Hokkien is spoken by more than 25 million people worldwide, yet remains under-represented in everyday writing. <strong>Hanri </strong>(<strong><span style=\"font-family:Sans-serif, Noto Sans TC\"><ruby style=\"position: relative;white-space: nowrap\">漢字<rt style=\"font-size: 60%;position: absolute;top: -1.2em;left: 0.55em\">한`띠ˉ</rt></ruby></span></strong>), or Chinese characters read through Hokkien, preserves meaning and lexical identity, but does not always make pronunciation clear. Romanisation shows pronunciation well, but sits outside the character-based writing tradition shared across East Asia.</p>\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://hokkienlang.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/vowels-illustration.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-3034\" style=\"width:125px;height:auto;float:right\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://hokkienlang.wordpress.com/tangliengim/\"><strong>Tangliengim</strong></a> (<strong><ruby style=\"position: relative;white-space: nowrap\">東寧音<rt style=\"font-size: 60%;position: absolute;top: -1.1em;left: 0.8em\">당ˉ롕임ˆ</rt></ruby></strong>) bridges these two functions.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Built on Hangul, Tangliengim uses phonetic blocks to represent Hokkien syllables, tones, and tone sandhi. It is designed primarily for <strong>Hanri–Hangul mixed writing</strong>: Hanri carries lexical meaning, while Hangul makes pronunciation explicit where useful. Pure Hangul remains available when fully phonetic writing is needed (e.g., in education).</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Same blocks, different sounds</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Take the word <strong>“student”</strong>:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li class=\"has-medium-font-size\">In Korean: <strong>학생</strong> (<em>hak-saeng</em>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li class=\"has-medium-font-size\">In Hokkien (written with Tangliengim): <strong><span style=\"font-family:Sans-serif, Noto Sans TC\"><ruby style=\"position: relative;white-space: nowrap\">學生<rt style=\"font-size: 60%;position: absolute;top: -1.2em;left: 0.72em\">학솅ˆ</rt></ruby></span></strong> (<em>hak-siêng</em>)</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">The blocks may look familiar, but the sound system is Hokkien. Tangliengim adapts Hangul’s syllable-based design to Hokkien phonology, especially its <strong>tones and tone sandhi</strong>, while working naturally alongside Hanri.</p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"margin-bottom: 2em\"></div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-default\" />\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\">Learn Tangliengim</h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-fe48e5de wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-fill\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-medium-blue-background-color has-background has-text-align-center has-medium-font-size has-custom-font-size wp-element-button\" href=\"https://hokkienlang.wordpress.com/tangliengim/\">Start learning in English</a></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-dark-gray-background-color has-background has-text-align-center has-medium-font-size has-custom-font-size wp-element-button\" href=\"https://hokkienlang.wordpress.com/zh-tw-tangliengim/\">以中文（繁）開始學習</a></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-fill\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-bright-blue-background-color has-background has-text-align-center has-medium-font-size has-custom-font-size wp-element-button\" href=\"https://hokkienlang.wordpress.com/zh-cn-tangliengim/\">以中文（简）开始学习</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"margin-bottom: 2em\"></div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-default\" />\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\">Guide to Hokkien tone sandhi</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Ready to go deeper?<br>Discover the tone-sandhi patterns that give Hokkien its distinctive rhythm.</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-fe48e5de wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--15\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-medium-font-size has-custom-font-size wp-element-button\" href=\"https://hokkienlang.wordpress.com/tone-sandhi-in-hokkien/\" style=\"padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)\">Tone sandhi in&nbsp;Hokkien</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"margin-bottom: 2em\"></div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\">Literature works</h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-small-font-size wp-duotone-unset-16\" style=\"min-height:430px;aspect-ratio:unset;\"><img data-attachment-id=\"3032\" data-permalink=\"https://hokkienlang.wordpress.com/the-egg/\" data-orig-file=\"https://hokkienlang.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/the-egg.png\" data-orig-size=\"707,841\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"The Egg\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://hokkienlang.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/the-egg.png?w=707\" data-cover-min-height=\"430\" class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-3032\" alt=\"\" src=\"https://hokkienlang.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/the-egg.png\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" /><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim-60 has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container is-layout-flow wp-block-cover-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-link-color has-large-font-size wp-elements-5 wp-block-paragraph\"><b><ruby style=\"font-family:Sans-serif, Noto Sans;position: relative;white-space: nowrap\" title=\"nn̄g\"><a href=\"/2025/01/26/the-egg/\">卵<rt style=\"font-size: 50%;position: absolute;top: -1.4em;left: 0.4em\">능ˉ</rt></a></ruby></b></p>\n</div></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" data-attachment-id=\"7199\" data-permalink=\"https://hokkienlang.wordpress.com/%e7%9b%ae%e9%8c%84-directory/naikiengki/\" data-orig-file=\"https://hokkienlang.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/naikiengki.png\" data-orig-size=\"1024,1024\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"naikiengki\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=